    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4f367a18_6708b960",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 15,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-09T12:15:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As I\u0027ve mentioned multiple times before, I\u0027d rather see us move our users away from `--bios` (to \"kernel mode\", crosvm\u0027s default) than implement yet another guest image loading layout, which we\u0027ll have to support.\n\nIn particular, I don\u0027t believe you can make this new layout the default (for BIOS mode) because that\u0027d break existing users and we have no exhaustive way to \"fix all the users\" because they might not be in AOSP; or am I missing something?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 15,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "7a5fc20e6d0c41c4f1de110c87b3064f2f476dab",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b79201c9_0558da05",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 15,
      "author": {
        "id": 1944400
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-09T18:30:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We should be able to get away with breaking people since we don\u0027t promise a stable VM platform yet. It isn\u0027t nice though.\n\nEventually we should add some kind of VM platform version that the user requests as part of spawning the VM. Maybe we can hold off on changing the default until we declare the first stable version.",
      "parentUuid": "4f367a18_6708b960",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 15,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "7a5fc20e6d0c41c4f1de110c87b3064f2f476dab",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "73ac3001_39522f0d",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 15,
      "author": {
        "id": 1944400
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-09T18:37:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m only just realizing now that we already have a \"platformVersion\" in the API and it at \"1.0\". I\u0027ve got some catching up to do.",
      "parentUuid": "b79201c9_0558da05",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 15,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "7a5fc20e6d0c41c4f1de110c87b3064f2f476dab",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fe84e3be_b7de481a",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 15,
      "author": {
        "id": 1944400
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-09T18:43:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Depending on how comfortable we are using that, we could declare something like version \"1.1\" just for the FDT change. If someone specifies \"1.0\", then they get the current behavior, if they specify \"1.1\", they get the new FDT behavior. Not in love with the idea, just musing.",
      "parentUuid": "73ac3001_39522f0d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 15,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "7a5fc20e6d0c41c4f1de110c87b3064f2f476dab",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "19d3d68f_813cb00e",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 15,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-10T02:35:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Let\u0027s not forget that custom VMs (Ferrochrome, and similar) are using and will be using `--bios`.\n\nIf I can decide, I\u0027d like to follow the memory layout of qemu as the default. That should be the least controversial option. What is it for arm64 bios mode?",
      "parentUuid": "fe84e3be_b7de481a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 15,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "7a5fc20e6d0c41c4f1de110c87b3064f2f476dab",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a54204cc_b98b3463",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 15,
      "author": {
        "id": 1944400
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-12T18:34:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "According to https://www.qemu.org/docs/master/system/arm/virt.html#hardware-configuration-information-for-bare-metal-programming, QEMU puts the device tree at the start of RAM for non-kernel guests. The start of RAM isn\u0027t the same location as in crosvm though (0x4000_0000 vs 0x8000_0000). It might load the BIOS binary into flash memory (not sure), which we don\u0027t have an equivalent to in crosvm.\n\nIn general, the qemu memory layout is going to differ from crosvm. I don\u0027t think it would be productive to try emulating it.",
      "parentUuid": "19d3d68f_813cb00e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 15,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "7a5fc20e6d0c41c4f1de110c87b3064f2f476dab",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "353c4d3c_7cf13741",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 15,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-13T00:56:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, we don\u0027t have to mimic qemu 100%, but what you researched sounds like Gunyah requiring payloads to be at the start of RAM is somewhat non-conventional, doesn\u0027t it?",
      "parentUuid": "a54204cc_b98b3463",
      "range": {
